{% extends "_base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Stage criteria · Private Inference Beat{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">Private Inference Beat stage criteria</h1>
<p class="mt-2 text-slate-600">Proposal draft-1 · no stages awarded. The current comparison publishes dated route assessments. This proposal makes the intended promotion criteria explicit for review before any ranking is introduced.</p>
<p class="mt-3 text-sm">Assess a specific endpoint, protocol, client version and mode, requested model, protected fields and all plaintext-holding components. A provider brand cannot inherit its best route's stage. Unassessed is a separate state; it is never an automatic Stage 0.</p>
<div class="overflow-x-auto mt-5"><table class="w-full text-sm text-left"><thead><tr class="border-b"><th class="p-2">Proposed stage</th><th class="p-2">Required evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr class="border-b align-top"><th class="p-2">Stage 0 · documented route</th><td class="p-2">A dated review names the client, plaintext holders, reference authority and unresolved obligations. At least one Stage 1 obligation is unmet or unknown. This is an inventory/assessment state, not a confidentiality guarantee.</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b align-top"><th class="p-2">Stage 1 · verified private route</th><td class="p-2">Every applicable obligation in all six <a href="./assessments.html#rubric" class="underline text-indigo-700">assessment axes</a> is Established with scoped proof records: hardware/TCB, live session and reply-key binding, approved reproducible code/model identity, operator-input constraints, downstream/request closure and explicit update authorization. N/A requires an architectural justification. Negative controls must reject substituted keys, models, workloads, stale evidence and unapproved updates before protected data leaves the client.</td></tr>
<tr class="border-b align-top"><th class="p-2">Stage 2 · independently sustained assurance</th><td class="p-2">Stage 1 plus independent build reproduction and route verification, a public versioned reference/update history with authenticated integrity and consistency checks, and an independently reviewed approval process that prevents unilateral operator updates from silently expanding client policy. Publish reviewers, trust roots, approval/revocation/rollback rules and evidence of enforcement.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p class="mt-4 text-sm">Promotion must record rubric version, reviewer, date, exact client and workload versions, policy authority/revision, proof records and test results. Reference changes trigger dependency review; neither new samples nor an unchanged hash renew an assessment. A stage describes only the recorded versions and scope.</p>
<p class="mt-3 text-sm">An adapter passing every configured check does not award a stage. Publication, provider authorization, analyst review and client acceptance remain independent facts. Historical audit-ledger verdicts do not award stages under this proposal.</p>
<p class="mt-3 text-sm">The current observatory retains evidence in Git; it does not provide a certificate-transparency protocol, append-only guarantees or log consistency proofs. Stage 2 is a proposed requirement, not a claim about this repository.</p>
<p class="mt-4"><a href="./index.html" class="underline text-indigo-700">Compare current route assessments</a></p>
{% endblock %}
